      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture. I'll improve understandability by: removing unused imports, splitting the monolithic `equals` test into focused, self-describing test methods, and using descriptive variable names.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports, splits the monolithic `equals` test into six focused, self-describing test methods (`clonedTagEqualsOriginal`, `tagDoesNotEqualNonTagObject`, `tagsWithDifferentNamespaceAreNotEqual`, etc.), and adds a brief comment in `canBeInsensitive` to clarify the intent of each assertion block — all while preserving exactly the same method calls, arguments, and expected outcomes."
